{"title":"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the following graph. Which of the following statements is true about the coordinates of the point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/d/a8d0c6b840a12d05c098bfea7ef89c07993e469b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x, y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/b/f5b16b499b02c6e4a860b846699b16cf90090828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{The values of both } x \\text{ and } y \\text{ are positive.} \\\\ \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\text{The value of } x \\text{ is positive and the value of } y \\text{ is negative.} \\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\text{The value of } x \\text{ is negative and the value of } y \\text{ is positive.} \\\\ \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\text{The values of both } x \\text{ and } y \\text{ are negative.} \\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{The value of } x \\text{ is } 0 \\text{ and the value of } y \\text{ is negative.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"98\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The point is to the right of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-coordinate must be positive. However, the point is also below the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis, so the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate must be negative.\n</p><p>This means that the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b48fce87e53f84dd785c1fb15c73eaa0e86bf4bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(B) } \\text{The value of } x \\text{ is positive and the value of } y \\text{ is negative.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"457\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)\">2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_7)_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 CEMC Gauss (Grade 7) Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/